<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44649" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sollemnĭtas</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sollenn-, solenn-</span></b> , and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">solemn-</span></b> ), ātis, f.
		sollemnis (postclass.; cf.: sollemne, celebratio). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A solemnity</i>, <i>festival</i>, <i>celebration</i> of a day: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dierum variae sollemnitates,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 2, 24, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pristina (ludorum Isthmiorum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">condendi honoris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Grat. Act. 36</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sacrorum sollemnitate prisco more completa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 23, 3, 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Deut. 16, 16</span></i> et
			saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A usage</i>, <i>formality</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					26, 8, 19</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">1, 7,
		25</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
